    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d488">

                <pb facs="0413" n="401" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg401"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 E. W. 1939/26011a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hibbard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-11-21T17:00:00-04:00">November 21,
                            1942—5 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>303. The Department would be interested in a summary of the reaction in Liberia
                    to the events which have taken place in North Africa.<anchor n="42"
                        xml:id="d488-f1"/> Has there been any change in the attitude of Liberian
                    officials toward the need of protection by United States defense forces?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d488-f1" n="42" xml:id="d488-f1-content">
                <p>Invasion by American forces beginning November 8, 1942; for correspondence, see
                        <ref target="frus1942v02#pg_429">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>,
                        pp. 429</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
